Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-17 (CC0 1.0: no rights
reserved) for the properties spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-
properties-rules-design.md on the site, section 6), no third-party content
but the shape of KiCad's Device:R as the drc-small fixture carries it, and a
ground symbol of our own (cc:GND). A KiCad 10 design with two variants:
- variants.kicad_sch, the root: R1 (10k, an MPN field), R2 (10k) and R3 (1k)
  in 0603, and #PWR01 (a power symbol, never a Fields row); in the variant
  Lite R2 is not fitted, in the variant Pro R3's value is 4k7 (each written
  inside the instance as KiCad 10 writes it);
- unfitted.kicad_sch, the sheet "Unfitted" (page 2), which carries its own
  do not populate: R4 (100k) inside it is not fitted in every variant;
- variants.kicad_pro names both variants with their descriptions;
- variants.kicad_pcb is the board as Update the board leaves it: the four
  footprints with their schematic paths, the board's variant list, R2's and
  R3's variant entries and R4 not populated. Nothing is wired: the parts
  stand alone, so the checks report their pins unconnected.
Read by kicad-cli 10.0.8 (kicad/kicad:10.0, 2026-11-17): the bill of
materials lists R4 DNP by default, R2 DNP under --variant Lite and R3 at 4k7
under --variant Pro. ids.json names the uuids for the tests. The KiCad files
carry no comment (their formats have none), so this file holds their license.
